From 362dc499674595e16879cb2b40fbfd909d7b7d9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/56] wifi: ath12k + PCI/pwrctrl: WCN7860 ("peach",
 17cb:110e)

Not upstream; carried from the OnePlus 15
port (infiniti-mainline/linux, branch oneplus-15), which has the same chip:

- 9cb8273bc "wifi: ath12k: add initial hardware definition for WCN7860"
  (Teguh Sobirin / Gianni Spadoni): hw params on the QCC2072 base, firmware
  dir WCN7860/hw2.0, M3 and aux ucode downloads. Its hw.c and core.h hunks
  did not apply here and were placed by hand (the enum value goes last).
- 7258d2605 "send QDSS config when CNSS_QDSS_CFG_MISS_V01 is disabled"
- b67592695 "disable CNSS_QDSS_CFG_MISS_V01 for the WCN7860" -- applied to
  the WCN7860 entry (applied blindly before the entry existed, it would hit
  QCC2072's instead)
- 348ad77eb "PCI/pwrctrl: pwrseq: add support for WCN7860": the pwrctrl
  driver must match pci17cb,110e or the host waits for it forever.

On TB323FU the chip does not enumerate yet; these compile
and the host bridge comes up.

[rebased onto 7.3: applied with fuzz (7.3 context: new QCC2072/IPQ5424 enum entries, qmi.c/qmi.h shifted)]
